id:                     E420
trigger_tool:           clang|make|autotools
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        wvSummary\.c.*incompatible integer to pointer conversion|gsf_doc_prop_get_val.*expression of type 'int'|gsf_doc_meta_data_new.*expression of type 'int'

severity:               2
category:               compat, headers, autotools, cross-compile
match_keywords:         legacy C, transitive declaration, implicit int, direct include, libgsf, gsf-doc-meta-data.h, wvSummary.c, int conversion
title:                  Legacy C sources must include the dependency header that owns each API declaration

root_cause:             A legacy C translation unit calls APIs declared by a dependency-specific public header but includes only neighboring headers that used to expose those declarations transitively. With a newer dependency header layout and modern Clang, the undeclared calls retain the legacy implicit-int type and fail when their results initialize pointer values.
affected_scope:         Legacy C and Autotools projects upgraded to newer dependency releases where public declarations were split into narrower headers, especially code compiled in C89 or -ansi mode.
verification_cmd:       Build the same source and dependency graph before and after adding only the owning public header; require the original undeclared-call pointer conversion to fail before, the translation unit to compile after, and the build to proceed beyond that object.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           include-api-owning-public-header
rec_description:        Identify the installed public header that declares every failing dependency API and include that header directly in the translation unit before rebuilding with the same compiler and dependency graph.
rec_command:            add #include <dependency/api-owner.h> to the translation unit and rebuild without diagnostic suppression
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      migrate-to-supported-dependency-api
fallback_description:   If the owning header proves the API was removed rather than merely split, migrate to the supported replacement under a dependency-version or feature check and add a focused consumer test.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       -Wno-(implicit-function-declaration|int-conversion)|-Wno-error=.*int-conversion
forbid_1_reason:        Diagnostic suppression preserves an incorrect implicit-int call signature instead of restoring the dependency API contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   Pointer return values can be truncated or misinterpreted, creating target-only crashes even when compilation is forced through.
forbid_2_pattern:       extern .*gsf_doc_(prop_get|meta_data)|manual prototype|forced include.*gsf-doc-meta-data
forbid_2_reason:        Handwritten declarations and global forced includes duplicate dependency ABI details outside the header that owns them.
forbid_2_consequence:   Future dependency updates can silently diverge from the copied signature or affect unrelated translation units.

principles:             P010, P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E081,E093,E309]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

